t(47, 935, """A: rabbit .. B: duck .. T: apple .. Th: garment.. Kindness to parents""")

t(47, 2020, """A: rabbit .. B: duck .. T: apple .. Th: garment .. Kindness to parents""")

t(48, 620, """A: rabbit .. B: duck .. T: apple .. Th: garment.. Kindness to parents""")

t(48, 1705, """A: rabbit .. B: duck .. T: apple .. Th: garment.. Kindness to parents""")

t(49, 280, """A: rabbit .. B: duck .. T: apple .. Th: garment.. Kindness to parents""")

t(49, 1365, """Do not lie against Allah, lest He destroy you with a punishment .. {"Musa said to them: Woe to you! Do not invent a lie against Allah, lest He destroy you with a punishment; and whoever invents has failed"}

Allah, our Great Lord, created fathers and mothers who are very good, like a breath of air .. and on the other hand He created fathers and mothers who are among the most evil of people on earth .. So how would Allah the Exalted lay down a rule of obedience? Where are your minds, O you who speak in da'wah?! Allah the Exalted laid down a balance; He did not lay down a fixed rule for evil fathers and mothers to use like a pickaxe to corrupt the earth and those upon it .. Far be it from Allah to give the evil ones on earth a deed from Him, hallowed be His names, so that they go about the earth corrupting it with an authority from Allah. For Allah the Exalted does not grant on His earth an authority that is used for injustice; He grants an authority with a balance, not an absolute authority. So He sent down the balance on earth and chose from His servants the prophets, the most pious of mankind and the purest of them absolutely; yet He did not permit them to demand from people that they obey them with absolute obedience, and permitted them only to demand absolute obedience from people in what was revealed to them. Have you heard of a prophet who forced a woman to marry him? For the marriage of any prophet is not part of legislation. Have you heard of a prophet who forced the owner of a house to sell him his house? Have you heard of a prophet who demanded people's obedience to him in what he had no right to? Have you heard of a prophet who asked a man to give him his mount or his horse? People were commanded to obey the prophets in legislation and in the charge that is from heaven .. So are fathers and mothers at a higher degree of goodness than the prophets, that they be given a deed of blind obedience? What is the matter with you, how do you judge, O callers to customs and the traditions of ignorance?! When our Great Lord, hallowed be His names, spoke in His Book of obedience to parents and mentioned the word obedience, it was only in a single verse, in which obedience came as something forbidden to do; so where are your minds and where is your reflection?! Did you not understand that the only verse in the Book of Allah that speaks of obedience to parents came in the form of not obeying, and not in the form of obeying? Do you not understand that this is a clear message from the Book of our Lord: do not invent in the religion of Allah what is not in it?! Why did you not reflect on the reason that obedience to parents exists in the Book of Allah in the negative and not in the affirmative? Because peoples had been written in the decree of Allah who would come and invent against the Book the opposite of what it brought. And the Book brought kindness (birr) to parents. And kindness to parents has a clear meaning .. Kindness contains a part of obedience in everything the parents need in matters particular to them, of their rights and their many private personal rights, of which I have spoken before here on the channel; and kindness means speaking with courtesy, gentleness and a lowered voice, praying for them, asking forgiveness for them, asking Allah's pardon for them, giving charity on their behalf living and dead, offering them every possible good in their lifetime, giving them gifts and meeting their needs.

In the picture is an example of one type of fathers and mothers .. We said there are the good and pure ones, may Allah preserve them all and bless their lives; but did Allah create all people good? So is this picture then reality or imagination? Is the existence of fathers and mothers who are not good reality or imagination?""")

t(50, 1000, """The general word, about a general situation and not describing a particular person: a fatwa in family matters is not by memorising the Qur'an, nor merely by preaching for fifty years, nor by memorising the books of fatwas .. A fatwa in family relations is something else .. something whose foundation must be firm in understanding the human soul .. and its branch in heaven, connected to the spirit of justice, and that no blame of any blamer should hold a person back for the sake of Allah .. A fatwa in family matters, in matters of paternal and maternal relations, family and children, and domestic and household disputes, is not by the social customs and traditions on which the one giving the fatwa was raised and grew up, because what he grew up on, which formed and shaped his thinking, is not necessarily sensitive to the balance of justice, the balance of rightness and the balance of wisdom! Therefore a fatwa on relations between family members, children with mothers and fathers, comes as a matter very hard to understand, even if the memoriser memorised the Book of Allah in full, memorised 100 thousand prophetic hadiths with sound chains, and memorised 10000 books on fiqh and fatwa .. None of that is proof of the soundness of giving people fatwas about right and wrong in the rights of people, of mothers, fathers and children .. The rights of fathers and mothers and the rights of children are a very thorny matter, the most dangerous matter in society absolutely, and one should not take it upon himself merely because the person is a sheikh with followers and must speak! No, you do not have to speak on everything .. You will not be a prophet, and it is natural that you will be right and be wrong .. so do not give fatwas on something you are not firmly grounded in.

The specific word: Unfortunately the influence of custom still clearly rules the mind, and hence what will be issued to people as a (fatwa), though the sheikh knows that the mufti is one who signs on behalf of the religion of Allah with an official signature .. It was not right that a questioner who says: if my mother orders me to do something wrong, do I obey her? be answered, O sheikh: if the wrong is slight, there is no harm! How strange! Is there slight and great in wrong? Otherwise the detail in classifying what harms and what does not harm is something on which speech is long and books are written .. So how are young people to distinguish between the harmful wrong and the non-harmful wrong, its types, its ranks, its shapes and its forms?!! And it was not for you, O sheikh, to tell people: if the mother insists on demanding that the wrong be done, say to her: fine, all right, Allah willing, do not worry; and then to tell people: and she will forget, and that is it, the problem ends! How did you know that she will forget? Glory be to Allah! How are catastrophic complications in homes, which have made the lives of sons and daughters a hell, answered with all this superficiality?!!! Many mistakes came in one of his clips .. And unfortunately, taking lightly the fatwa on personal relations between holders of rights is a taking-lightly that has destroyed the Ummah; and what I see clearly is that it is a real disregard for the rights of people, fathers and mothers on one side and sons and daughters on the other, a clear flattening of the problems and an offering of solutions that have no relation to reality and solve no problem. This flattening is the cause of the continuation of problems in homes, and the cause of the continuation of disasters and the cause of the calamities that never stop in the homes of Muslims; and the cause of that is none other than the mistaken understanding of the meaning of kindness to parents, or the correct understanding together with the fear of breaking social custom and placing it above religion. And in the sheikh I see only the first as a cause, which is the incorrect understanding of the meaning of kindness to parents.

Accordingly, as for the sheikh, and may he permit me, no courtesy will keep me from the truth; the sheikh gives fatwas to people publicly, and the correction must be public. The sheikh does not know how to distinguish between kindness to parents and obedience to parents; this is not ignorance but the dominance of customs and traditions over the mind, which did not allow the mind to grasp well the meanings of the Book of Allah. The sheikh confuses kindness with obedience; and you, may Allah bless you, have a very clear confusion about the concept of kindness and the inclusion of obedience in kindness, whereas obedience is a part of kindness and kindness is not obedience. The sheikh is unfortunately still, like many others, under the influence of custom, customs and traditions that have no relation, near or far, to Islamic legislation in what governs the conduct of motherhood and fatherhood with children! The sheikh presents kindness to his followers as being obedience to parents, and this is a disaster; we are still forced every day to come out and repeat what we have said a thousand times: kindness has no relation to obedience, and I have explained this matter here on the channel time and time again

Finally, a general word: ((some)) of the preachers who speak to people, and those people who listen to them, are themselves lost; they do not understand the meaning of the kindness and good treatment that our Great Lord, hallowed be His names, commanded us in His Book, and they still present it to people as being obedience!!!!!! And here is the breach through which the Ummah was reached in its homes, and this was the breach through which Satan""")

t(51, 60, """entered to shatter the Ummah and gnaw it from within (the homes). And for the millionth time: kindness contains a part of obedience in everything the parents need in matters particular to them, of their rights and their many private personal rights, of which I have spoken before here on the channel; and kindness means speaking with courtesy, gentleness and a lowered voice, praying for them, asking forgiveness for them, asking Allah's pardon for them, giving charity on their behalf living and dead, and offering them every possible good in their lifetime. As for obedience in anything that is not among the rights of fathers and mothers, the Book of Allah is innocent of it, Islam is innocent of it, and the Prophet ﷺ is innocent of it .. There is no obedience to parents in what is not among their rights. There came in the Book of Allah a single verse on obedience to parents in which the word obedience is mentioned, and it came in the form of forbidding obedience in associating partners with Allah. And the strangest of the strange is that we find preachers who see associating partners with Allah as a wrong with which one must not obey the parents, yet they do not see injustice as the brother of shirk; so the children are told: obey your fathers and mothers in what contains injustice, as if injustice were not the brother of shirk .. Injustice is the brother of shirk, its paternal cousin and its maternal cousin. Injustice means worshipping desire instead of Allah ... it means worshipping the father instead of Allah .. it means worshipping the mother instead of Allah .. Our Great Lord, hallowed be His names, forbade obedience to parents if they order us to prostrate to an idol, and it is a verse of clear, explicit text; and what if they order us to prostrate to them themselves with the prostration of shirk? The father who says to his son: divorce your wife, is a father who wants his son to prostrate to him with the prostration of shirk. The mother who asks her son to divorce his wife is a mother who wants her son to prostrate to her with the prostration of shirk. The father who orders his son to sit with him and listen to his backbiting of people and his insulting them, and if he does not do so he is an undutiful son, is a father who asks his son to prostrate to him with the prostration of shirk, because Allah the Exalted has forbidden us injustice. So whose word do we hear? And whom shall we obey? Therefore, enough toying with the Ummah.""")

t(51, 1735, """Do not be heedless of your children .. The price may be an entire lifetime .. The decrees of Allah come to pass .. Even so, do not be heedless of your children .. In a moment you are unaware of they may snatch away an entire lifetime while they are among you and with you""")

t(52, 1395, """Two days ago one of the followers wrote here about al-Burhan that he is an atheist .. And now a video of al-Burhan appeared to me in which he praises Allah, our Great Lord, and sends prayers and peace upon His Messenger ﷺ. I cannot understand this childish business, how long will it go on .. Do you think you are in the sixties, broadcasting us a news item, say, from a state channel and telling us so-and-so is an atheist and so-and-so is a disbeliever? Why do you disgrace yourselves, brother.. Brother, fear Allah concerning yourselves, brother""")

t(53, 90, """My Lord, make it come true .. The return of those scattered in the corners of the world to their families .. willingly, by Allah's leave, or by force .. It does not matter .. and it is not important""")

t(53, 1215, """A little girl running toward her mother after years of the mother being deprived of her daughter by her unjust ex-husband""")

t(53, 2290, """The only solution to be rid of this picture is to return people to their countries and homelands, so that they live among their families and in the midst of their loved ones, by soft power or by overwhelming power, even if by coercion .. No difference .. no difference .. no difference .. What matters is that the bleeding of the weary, bleeding souls of Muslims stops .. their separation from their kin .. the ache of their hearts by night and by day .. their grief by night and by day .. their being deprived of living as human beings .. Even the animal has its young living with it .. And it is a human right to have a life in which fathers and mothers are near their children.""")

t(54, 1060, """After the Third World War""")

t(54, 2140, """During the Third World War""")
